        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0440" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg356"/>

                <head>No. 174.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 13,
                        1886</date>. [Received September 27.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 351.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith a copy of a note sent by me to Lord Iddesleigh, Her Majesty’s secretary
                    of state for foreign affairs, under date of September 11, 1886, on the subject
                    of the Canadian fisheries.</p>
                <p>And I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>E. J. PHELPS.</signed></closer>






